  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Soon, IMU trackers will be more readily available. If you could please set a standard for listening for FBT signals, whether over network, background app, or from a remote Virtual/low powered pc. (Example: SlimeVR might be able to make a background app to feed headset/controller position info to a PC to math out the IK positions of the virtual trackers, and then sending that back to the background app and shared locally to a port / protocol/standard you set.)\nCombined with my other request to listen to OSC type data for Quest Pro on standalone, you’d potentially get 11 point Face and Eye tracking available while on the road with a Quest pro, a bunch of slimes, and a really good internet connection (or a potato work laptop)\nMeta mentioned VRChat during the Quest Pro launch, I think this type of setup would be reasonable for most folks that travel a lot for work, and still want to hang out in FBT without having to a lug a couple base stations and a bunch of power bricks and small stands everywhere you go. Would also show to Meta that people think legs are important, even if it’s an add-on accessory.",
